BDDWorkflow -[hidden]- Comparison
Comparison -[hidden]- Benefits

' Legend
legend right
  <b>BDD with JBehave - Component Summary</b>

  <b>Story Files (.story):</b>
  Natural language scenarios using Gherkin
  syntax. Written in Given-When-Then format.
  Readable by non-technical stakeholders.

  <b>Step Definitions:</b>
  Java classes with @Given/@When/@Then
  annotations. Map steps to code.
  Bridge between language and implementation.

  <b>BDD Implementation:</b>
  Business logic that implements
  behavior described in scenarios.
  Focus on business value.

  <b>Domain Models:</b>
  Business entities (Deal, Plan, etc.)
  used in scenarios. Reflect real-world
  concepts.

  <b>JBehave Runner:</b>
  Configures and executes stories.
  Generates test reports.

  <b>JBehave Framework:</b>
  Parses Gherkin, matches steps,
  executes scenarios, generates reports.

  <b>Key Insight:</b>
  BDD is about communication and
  collaboration, not just testing.
  Scenarios facilitate discussions
  that build shared understanding.
endlegend

@enduml